on all three hosts by rule name). Note the JS/Dart construction caveats you already found (float64-from-bits, explicit float64). (2) Apply the P3 pointer fixes of Part 3 (UCF 7.11 clause 10 pointer, linker.md :243 wording, linearize_test.cljc:286 retarget, and every other P3 the report lists, including the parity_test continuation-line columns via `cljstyle fix` on the changed files). (3) Ledger: close the binder row with the Architect's exact wording; reopen/close the decode* row with the report's wording (item 7); leave other rows as round 1 had them. Stage NOTHING; but organise the working tree so the Architect's two-commit split is easy: Part 1(a)+its test+malformed_rows+row 25 are one logical commit (code), Parts 2 and 3 are the other(s); state in the report which files belong to which. NOT allowed: src/yang, test/yang, scanner_goldens, pinned goldens/descriptors, collab commits; if ANY pinned byte moves (cbor conformance digest, fixtures), STOP and report. Foreground lanes: kondo on changed files (0 errors/warnings/infos); focused `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.ucf.remote-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-test -n yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.semantic.frame-test -n yin.vm.semantic.parity-test -n yin.vm.host-typed-values-test -n dao.jing.cbor-test` plus any dao.jing conformance namespace that loads cbor (run `-r '^dao\\.jing\\..*'`); then the whole JVM quick tier `clojure -M:test -e :slow` (unrestricted). Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-followup-2.report.md with Completed-GMT/Completed-Local/Coding-Agent/Session-ID, per-step results, counts, mutants (which hosts each mutant would die on), file-to-commit mapping, truthful. End READY or BLOCKED.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
